# Match-play types & reporting generalization

Lessons from format editor / H2H / live-scores hardening: generalize presentation by
**shared adapters and query keys**, never by a second client ranking or fiction settings.

## Backend owns winners and structure

Winners, series resolution, advancement, and match-structure sync are API/backend only
(`no-client-engines.mdc`). Allowed on the client: diagram/scoring adapters, labels,
manual-winner UX that calls the API, and print formatting of API JSON.

## Fiction config is unfinished surface

Do not seed or edit UI for `competition_method_config` keys the backend does not apply
(e.g. unwired `selection_mode`, `bye_criteria`, DYLG advertising when forced off). Prefer
backend defaults / strip-on-save over shipping controls that only write JSON.

## One React Query key per resource

The same list endpoint must not use two cache keys (e.g. `roundRelationships` vs
`tournamentFlowRelationships`). Invalidation helpers (`eventFlowQueries`) and Event Details /
flow preview must share one key or views go stale after format apply.

## Route by method; don’t mount unused work

Format Matchups and scoring surfaces should early-return by `competition_method` so RR
hooks/queries are not mounted for bracket/stepladder (and vice versa). Shared hooks
(`useFormatEditorMatchupQueries`) are for identical query blocks, not for loading every
method’s UI at once.

## Shared identity across scoring diagrams and reports

Participant slot id / option resolve / “TBD” labels belong in one helper path used by
match-play diagram adapters, scoring visuals, and report builders. Do not invent a third
side-label map for print.

## Reports: registry + print kit only

New director sheets = menu def + API fetch + thin `build*ReportDocument` on the shared
print kit (`report-registry.mdc`, `print-report-kit.mdc`). No counting rules in builders;
no one-off `@page`/logo CSS.
